# azzamadie-portfolio — Project rules

## Stack

- Static HTML/CSS/vanilla JS. No React, no bundler unless explicitly requested.
- GSAP + ScrollTrigger from CDN; page animations in `pages.js`, globals in `app.js`.
- Blog/CV data via `supabase-client.js` and Supabase JS v2 CDN.

## Code style

- Minimize diff scope; match existing naming and file layout.
- Prefer extending `supabase-client.js` helpers over duplicating fetch/error logic.
- Magnetic hover: wrap controls in `magnetic-wrap`; do not rely on `data-magnetic` alone.
- Before ScrollTrigger animations, verify targets exist (About: `.about-lab__visual`, `.about-pivot__equation`).
- Blog category filters use category **name** (stored on posts), not slug.

## Security

- Anon key in client is OK; never commit service role keys or `.env`.
- Admin password in `admin.html` / `editor.html` is client-only — recommend Supabase Auth for real protection.

## Verification

- Serve with `python -m http.server 8765` (not `file://`).
- After changes, spot-check affected pages and browser console.

## Commits

- Only commit when the user asks.
- Message style: `fix:`, `feat:`, `content:`, `docs:` with a short why.
